  "question": {
    "text": "The sum of all integral values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> for which the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> has no real roots, is_____.",
    "image": null
